  "id": "shin-splints",
  "name": "Shin splints (medial tibial stress syndrome)",
  "kind": "FOCUSED",
  "category": "REHAB",
  "goal": "Ease shin pain by adjusting your running load and building the calf and foot strength that absorbs each landing, then return to running gradually.",
  "whoFor": "Runners and walkers with an ache along the inside edge of the shin bone, spread over several centimetres, that comes on with running.",
  "notFor": [
    "Pain in one small spot on the bone (possible stress fracture): see a doctor"
  ],
  "estMinutes": 15,
  "trackedMetric": "Shin pain during or after running or walking (0-10)",
  "painRules": "Cut running back to a level that keeps shin pain at 2-3 out of 10 or less and settled by the next day. Strength work should not increase shin pain.",
  "redFlags": [
    "Pain in one small spot on the shin bone that hurts to press, hop or at rest (possible stress fracture)",
    "Pain at night or at rest",
    "Tightness, burning, numbness or weakness in the lower leg that builds during exercise and eases with rest",
    "Swelling, redness or warmth of the shin"
  ],
